  "slug": "scientific-fair-5429",
  "summary": "New methods enumerate ambiguous metastatic migration histories and separate lineage from microenvironment effects in spatial tumor data.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is reconstructing history and structure in tumors from static, spatially or genomically resolved measurements while making the inferential uncertainty explicit. MACH2 enumerates all optimal metastatic migration histories from DNA sequencing and adds a clone-location parsimony criterion, so the solution space is characterized rather than a single history reported. SOUR separates heritable lineage contributions from spatial microenvironment contributions to tumor cell expression in spatial lineage tracing data. SpaDAG learns spatially varying causal DAGs on tissue triangulations in spatial transcriptomics using MCMC sampling. An ABC, sequential Monte Carlo and random forest pipeline ranks parameters in spatiotemporal agent-based tumor models. The new emphasis is on ambiguity and on partitioning inherited from environmental variation.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
